+++ b/docs/creation-binding.md
@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+# Atomic task creation
+
+This local compatibility patch implements the Store prerequisite of autosk-flow
+issue 11. It does not establish full workflow, sandbox, or release acceptance.
+
+## API map
+
+The Go CLI is a JSON-RPC client. Autoskd owns task state. The existing Unix socket
+and authenticated TCP transport are reused; no service or port is added.
+
+| Caller | Method | Input | Success | Failure |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Legacy CLI/clients | `task.create` | `cwd`, `title`, optional `description`, `blocked_by` | Existing `TaskView` | Existing RPC errors; creation markers are rejected |
+| Operator CLI/clients | `task.create_bound` | Same input plus required `creation_key`, `creation_binding_hash` | `TaskCreationResult` | Structured `conflict` or `invalid` details |
+| Trusted host code | `Store.createTaskWithCreationBinding` | `TaskCreationInput`, bound to one Store | `TaskCreationResult` | `TaskCreationError` |
+| Model MCP tools | Existing legacy creation surface | Existing model tool schema | Existing task projection | Reserved creation markers are unavailable |
+
+`TaskCreationResult` contains exactly `outcome` and `task`. Successful outcomes are
+`created` and `existing_same_binding`. The task projection contains exactly `id`,
+`status`, `workflow`, `step`, `title`, `description`, `blocked_by`, `creation_key`,
+and `creation_binding_hash`; blockers are task IDs, and absent workflow/step are
+JSON null. Store errors preserve a stable reason and conflict identity in the RPC
+error details. A malformed request returns `INVALID_PARAMS`; a binding conflict
+returns `CONFLICT`. Unknown storage failures remain errors, never successful
+creation results.
+
+`autosk create --creation-key KEY --creation-binding-hash HASH --json` uses the
+bound method. Both flags are required together. Without either flag, existing
+CLI behavior and JSON output remain compatible. Bound creation rejects
+`--workflow` and `--blocks` before opening a client: these are separate side
+effects and cannot be represented as an atomic creation receipt. Operators can
+perform enrollment or reverse-blocker changes explicitly after creation.
+
+Reusing a key with the same binding returns the original task. Display edits do
+not change creation identity. A different binding conflicts. Deleted task keys
+cannot silently name a replacement task. Updating or importing creation markers
+through ordinary mutable task fields is forbidden.
+
+## Storage and build layout
+
+Autoskd validates creation semantics and owns the reservation index under
+`.autosk/creation/v1/`. Its `autosk-store-lock` child holds a project lock and
+executes the corresponding file reads and writes through directory handles.
+The helper receives JSON lines over private stdin/stdout; it has no listening
+socket, task scheduler, or independent task semantics. Keeping the lock and
+file operations in the same process prevents a surviving JavaScript callback
+from writing after the lock-holding process has died.
+
+Creation first saves a pending reservation with the chosen task ID, then writes
+the complete task record with both markers, then activates the reservation.
+Pending tasks are excluded from task views and scheduling. Retry finishes the
+same reservation. Active reservations whose tasks have been removed become
+tombstones; a tombstone cannot allocate another task ID for that key.
+
+`make build-autoskd` builds both `bin/autoskd` and `bin/autosk-store-lock`.
+`scripts/package-autoskd.sh PREFIX` places both executables in `PREFIX/bin`;
+`make install-autoskd` installs both in the configured Go binary directory.
+The compiled daemon locates the helper beside its own executable. Source-level
+tests set `AUTOSK_STORE_LOCK_BIN` to an explicitly built helper. Bun and Go are
+build dependencies; the installed pair does not require either runtime.
+
+This patch is a prerequisite, not the complete filesystem boundary of issue 13.
+Workflow preflight, pinned helper/distribution identity, capability-scoped SDK
+integration, and an approved distribution path remain autosk-flow obligations.
+
+## Required verification
+
+Tests must cover the actual Store and JSON-RPC transport, CLI JSON parity,
+concurrent clients, changed binding, malformed input, project isolation, lost
+response/retry, restart, immutable marker edits, deletion and corrupt records.
+Transport doubles test serialization only. New focused daemon smoke and RPC
+tests use an isolated home and socket, disabled bootstrap installation, and
+loopback-only or disabled TCP. Older upstream Go auto-spawn tests use an isolated
+home and token but retain the default TCP listener. A successful RPC response
+does not establish power-loss durability.
+Focused CLI smoke starts a compiled daemon with temp `HOME`, explicit temp
+socket, `AUTOSK_NO_AUTO_INSTALL=1`, and `--tcp 127.0.0.1:0`.
